<p>When transporting your bike from Bihar to Coimbatore, it is essential to have the following documents prepared:</p>

<p>The original Registration Certificate (RC) is crucial as proof of ownership. However, for transit purposes, a self-attested photocopy of the RC should be prepared.</p>

<p>The Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate ensures that your bike meets emission standards. A valid PUC, with an expiry date not exceeding 30 days, is mandatory for transport.</p>

<p>An active insurance certificate is necessary to cover any potential damages or accidents during transit. Ensure that the insurance has been renewed and provides comprehensive coverage for the bike.</p>

<p>The IBA (Indian Billing Association) Approved Consignment Bill of Lading is a document that outlines the details of the shipment, including the sender, receiver, vehicle description, and estimated transit time.</p>

